.Dd October 10, 2026
.Dt PKG-AUTOUPGRADE 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pkg autoupgrade
.Nd automated package upgrade with safety net and service restart
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm pkg autoupgrade
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
command is provided by the
.Em autoupgrade
plugin for
.Xr pkg 8 .
It performs an unattended package upgrade with the following steps:
.Bl -enum
.It
Refresh the catalogs of all allowed repositories.
.It
Build and solve an upgrade job.
If
.Ev AU_ALLOW_BASE_UPGRADE
is false, repositories listed in
.Ev AU_BASE_REPOS
are excluded so that pkgbase (kernel, world) packages are not upgraded
automatically.
.It
Before applying the job, create a safety net:
.Bl -dash -compact
.It
.Em ZFS root :
create a boot environment via
.Xr libbe 3
named
.Dq Ar prefix Ns - Ns Ar YYYYMMDDTHHmmSS .
Old auto-created environments are pruned to
.Ev AU_BE_KEEP
entries.
.It
.Em UFS root :
if a kernel package is being upgraded and
.Ev AU_UFS_KERNEL_BACKUP
is true, rename
.Pa /boot/kernel
to
.Pa /boot/kernel.old .
The boot loader can boot from
.Pa /boot/kernel.old
via the
.Dq Boot Older Kernel
menu entry or
.Xr nextboot 8 .
.El
.It
Apply the upgrade job.
.It
Detect services that need restarting using two methods:
.Bl -dash -compact
.It
.Em Direct rc ownership :
for each script in
.Pa /etc/rc.d/
and
.Pa /usr/local/etc/rc.d/ ,
query which package owns it via
.Xr pkgdb 8 .
If the owning package was upgraded, the service is a candidate.
.It
.Em Stale mapping scan :
enumerate running processes via
.Xr libprocstat 3 .
Any process with an executable VNODE mapping whose path is absent from the
kernel name cache is using a stale binary or shared library
(the file was replaced on disk while the process held an open inode mapping).
If the process
.Em comm
name matches an rc script, that service is a candidate.
This detects the shared-library upgrade case (e.g.\& openssl upgraded,
nginx still maps old libssl.so).
.El
For each candidate service that is currently running:
.Bl -dash -compact
.It
If it appears in
.Ev AU_RESTART_SERVICES ,
restart it via
.Dq service Ar name restart .
.It
Otherwise, append a pending notice to
.Pa /var/run/motd .
.El
.It
Packages whose names match a pattern in
.Ev AU_BLOCKLISTED_PACKAGES
are removed from the upgrade job before it is applied.
.It
If a kernel package was upgraded and the system is not inside a jail:
.Bl -dash -compact
.It
If
.Ev AU_ALLOW_REBOOT
is true and no interactive users are logged in (or
.Ev AU_REBOOT_IF_USERS_LOGGED_IN
is true), reboot at the time specified by
.Ev AU_REBOOT_TIME .
.It
If
.Ev AU_ALLOW_REBOOT
is true but users are logged in and
.Ev AU_REBOOT_IF_USERS_LOGGED_IN
is false, defer the reboot and write a notice to
.Pa /var/run/motd .
.It
If
.Ev AU_ALLOW_REBOOT
is false, write a reboot-required notice to
.Pa /var/run/motd .
.El
.It
If
.Ev AU_AUTOREMOVE
is true, remove orphaned packages via
.Dq pkg autoremove .
.El
Notices written to
.Pa /var/run/motd
are also persisted in
.Pa /var/db/pkg-autoupgrade/notices
so that the
.Em pkg_autoupgrade_motd
.Xr rc 8
service can re-stamp
.Pa /var/run/motd
after the system
.Em motd
service regenerates it at the next boot.
.Sh CONFIGURATION
The plugin reads
.Pa /usr/local/etc/pkg/autoupgrade.conf
in UCL format.
The file is optional; compiled-in defaults are used when it is absent.
.Bl -tag -width "AU_RESTART_SERVICES"
.It Ev AU_ALLOW_BASE_UPGRADE
Boolean.
Allow upgrading pkgbase (FreeBSD base system) packages.
Default:
.Cm false .
.It Ev AU_BASE_REPOS
String (comma-separated).
Repository names that contain base system packages.
Used only when
.Ev AU_ALLOW_BASE_UPGRADE
is false.
Default:
.Cm "FreeBSD-base" .
.It Ev AU_BE_ENABLED
Boolean.
Create a boot environment before each upgrade run (ZFS only).
Default:
.Cm true .
.It Ev AU_BE_PREFIX
String.
Prefix for auto-created boot environment names.
Default:
.Cm "pre-autoupgrade" .
.It Ev AU_BE_KEEP
Integer >= 1.
Maximum number of auto-created boot environments to retain.
Default:
.Cm 5 .
.It Ev AU_UFS_KERNEL_BACKUP
Boolean.
On UFS roots, back up
.Pa /boot/kernel
to
.Pa /boot/kernel.old
before a kernel upgrade.
Default:
.Cm true .
.It Ev AU_ALLOW_REBOOT
Boolean.
Automatically reboot after a kernel upgrade (not inside a jail).
Default:
.Cm false .
.It Ev AU_RESTART_SERVICES
String (comma-separated).
Services that may be restarted automatically.
All other affected services receive only a MOTD notice.
Default: empty (no automatic restarts).
.It Ev AU_ONLY_UPGRADE_VULNERABLE_PKG
Boolean.
When true, only packages with known vulnerabilities (per
.Xr pkg-audit 8 )
are upgraded.
The vulnerability database is refreshed automatically before each run.
If no vulnerable packages are found the run is a no-op.
.Ev AU_ALLOW_BASE_UPGRADE
and
.Ev AU_BASE_REPOS
are still respected.
Default:
.Cm false .
.It Ev AU_BLOCKLISTED_PACKAGES
String (comma-separated POSIX extended regular expressions).
Package names matching any of these patterns are excluded from the upgrade job.
Patterns are anchored only if the expression itself includes
.Sq ^
or
.Sq $ .
To permanently pin a package, prefer
.Xr pkg-lock 8 ;
this setting applies to automated runs only and user-locked packages are
always respected regardless.
Default: empty (no packages excluded).
.It Ev AU_AUTOREMOVE
Boolean.
Run
.Dq pkg autoremove
after a successful upgrade to remove orphaned packages.
Default:
.Cm false .
.It Ev AU_REBOOT_TIME
String.
When
.Ev AU_ALLOW_REBOOT
is true, controls when the system reboots after a kernel upgrade.
.Cm now
reboots immediately via
.Xr reboot 2 .
An
.Cm HH:MM
value schedules the reboot via
.Xr shutdown 8
so that logged-in users receive advance notice.
Default:
.Cm "now" .
.It Ev AU_REBOOT_IF_USERS_LOGGED_IN
Boolean.
When
.Ev AU_ALLOW_REBOOT
is true and interactive users are logged in, controls whether the reboot
proceeds anyway.
When false (the default), the reboot is deferred and a MOTD notice is written
instead so that no active session is dropped unexpectedly.
Default:
.Cm false .
.It Ev AU_MAIL_TO
String.
Email address for post-upgrade reports.
Requires a working MTA with a
.Xr sendmail 8 Ns -compatible
interface at
.Pa /usr/sbin/sendmail .
Empty (the default) disables email notifications.
.It Ev AU_MAIL_REPORT
String.
Controls when email reports are sent.
.Cm always
sends after every run.
.Cm on-change
(the default) sends when at least one package was upgraded.
.Cm on-error
sends only when an error occurred.
Default:
.Cm "on-change" .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/usr/local/etc/pkg/autoupgrade.conf.sample"
.It Pa /usr/local/etc/pkg/autoupgrade.conf
Plugin configuration (UCL).
.It Pa /usr/local/lib/pkg/autoupgrade.so
Plugin shared object loaded by
.Xr pkg 8 .
.It Pa /var/run/motd
Pending notices are written here in a delimited section.
.It Pa /var/db/pkg-autoupgrade/notices
Persistent copy of pending notices; repopulated at boot.
.El
.Sh PERIODIC INTEGRATION
Enable the daily run by adding the following to
.Pa /etc/periodic.conf ,
.Pa /etc/periodic.conf.local ,
or
.Pa /usr/local/etc/periodic.conf :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
daily_pkg_autoupgrade_enable="YES"
.Ed
.Pp
The periodic script is installed at
.Pa /usr/local/etc/periodic/daily/500.pkg-autoupgrade .
.Sh ENABLING THE PLUGIN
Add the plugin to
.Pa /usr/local/etc/pkg.conf :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
PLUGINS [ "autoupgrade" ];
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pkg 8 ,
.Xr pkg.conf 5 ,
.Xr libbe 3 ,
.Xr periodic 8 ,
.Xr service 8 ,
.Xr nextboot 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
plugin first appeared in the pkg-autoupgrade project, 2026.
